# CrossEngin domain pack: biology fundamentals (v1)
#
# ~70 atoms + ~70 implications covering the stable core of
# undergraduate biology: taxonomy of life, cell types, organelles,
# key molecules, organ systems, biological processes, foundational
# figures, milestone dates.
#
# Standard reference sources: Campbell Biology, Alberts Molecular
# Biology of the Cell, NCBI Taxonomy, ICZN nomenclature.
#
# EDITORIAL STANCE:
#   * Descriptive science content at the level a well-vetted textbook
#     would present today. Ontological is-a edges (a mitochondrion IS
#     an organelle; a human IS a mammal) get FORMAL strength because
#     those are stable taxonomic categorizations.
#   * Empirical claims about processes (photosynthesis produces oxygen)
#     get EMPIRICAL strength -- the mechanism is well-established but
#     phrased as evidence-supported, not proved-in-the-kernel.
#   * Belief grades reflect scientific consensus. Well-attested claims
#     (DNA is a double helix; humans are eukaryotes) at 1000; things
#     with genuine measurement debate (exact number of human genes)
#     could go lower -- this pack focuses on unambiguous content only.
#
# Ingest via:
#   /ingest cerec data/packs/biology.cerec biology src:pack:biology:v1

KG biology
SRC src:pack:biology:v1

# ============================================================================
# 1. Root ontology
# ============================================================================

ATOM living_thing 3 1000
ATOM organism 3 1000
ATOM cell 3 1000
ATOM tissue 3 950
ATOM organ 3 950
ATOM organ_system 3 950
ATOM molecule 3 1000
ATOM biological_process 3 950
ATOM taxonomic_rank 3 950
ATOM organelle 3 950
ATOM person 3 950
ATOM historical_event 3 950

IMP organism living_thing FORMAL
IMP cell living_thing FORMAL
IMP tissue cell EMPIRICAL
IMP organ tissue EMPIRICAL
IMP organ_system organ EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 2. The three domains of life
# ============================================================================

ATOM bacteria 3 1000
ATOM archaea 3 1000
ATOM eukarya 3 1000

IMP bacteria organism FORMAL
IMP archaea organism FORMAL
IMP eukarya organism FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 3. Kingdoms of eukarya
# ============================================================================

ATOM animalia 3 1000
ATOM plantae 3 1000
ATOM fungi 3 950
ATOM protista 3 900

IMP animalia eukarya FORMAL
IMP plantae eukarya FORMAL
IMP fungi eukarya FORMAL
IMP protista eukarya FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 4. Taxonomic ranks (ontological hierarchy)
# ============================================================================

ATOM domain 3 950
ATOM kingdom 3 950
ATOM phylum 3 950
ATOM class_rank 3 950
ATOM order_rank 3 950
ATOM family_rank 3 950
ATOM genus 3 950
ATOM species 3 950

IMP domain taxonomic_rank FORMAL
IMP kingdom taxonomic_rank FORMAL
IMP phylum taxonomic_rank FORMAL
IMP class_rank taxonomic_rank FORMAL
IMP order_rank taxonomic_rank FORMAL
IMP family_rank taxonomic_rank FORMAL
IMP genus taxonomic_rank FORMAL
IMP species taxonomic_rank FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 5. Selected representative organisms
# ============================================================================

ATOM human 1 1000
ATOM chimpanzee 1 950
ATOM dog 1 1000
ATOM cat 1 1000
ATOM oak_tree 1 900
ATOM e_coli 1 950
ATOM saccharomyces_cerevisiae 1 900

IMP human animalia FORMAL
IMP chimpanzee animalia FORMAL
IMP dog animalia FORMAL
IMP cat animalia FORMAL
IMP oak_tree plantae FORMAL
IMP e_coli bacteria FORMAL
IMP saccharomyces_cerevisiae fungi FORMAL

ATOM mammal 3 950
ATOM primate 3 950
IMP mammal animalia FORMAL
IMP primate mammal FORMAL
IMP human mammal EMPIRICAL
IMP human primate EMPIRICAL
IMP chimpanzee mammal EMPIRICAL
IMP chimpanzee primate EMPIRICAL
IMP dog mammal EMPIRICAL
IMP cat mammal EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 6. Cell types + organelles
# ============================================================================

ATOM prokaryote 3 950
ATOM eukaryote 3 950
ATOM animal_cell 3 950
ATOM plant_cell 3 950

IMP prokaryote cell FORMAL
IMP eukaryote cell FORMAL
IMP animal_cell eukaryote EMPIRICAL
IMP plant_cell eukaryote EMPIRICAL

ATOM nucleus 3 950
ATOM mitochondria 3 950
ATOM chloroplast 3 950
ATOM ribosome 3 950
ATOM golgi_apparatus 3 900
ATOM endoplasmic_reticulum 3 900

IMP nucleus organelle FORMAL
IMP mitochondria organelle FORMAL
IMP chloroplast organelle FORMAL
IMP ribosome organelle FORMAL
IMP golgi_apparatus organelle FORMAL
IMP endoplasmic_reticulum organelle FORMAL

IMP chloroplast plant_cell EMPIRICAL
IMP mitochondria animal_cell EMPIRICAL
IMP mitochondria plant_cell EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 7. Key molecules
# ============================================================================

ATOM dna 1 1000
ATOM rna 1 1000
ATOM protein 1 1000
ATOM amino_acid 1 950
ATOM atp 1 1000
ATOM glucose 1 1000
ATOM lipid 3 950
ATOM enzyme 3 950

IMP dna molecule FORMAL
IMP rna molecule FORMAL
IMP protein molecule FORMAL
IMP amino_acid molecule FORMAL
IMP atp molecule FORMAL
IMP glucose molecule FORMAL
IMP enzyme protein EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 8. Organ systems (human/mammalian)
# ============================================================================

ATOM nervous_system 3 1000
ATOM circulatory_system 3 1000
ATOM respiratory_system 3 1000
ATOM digestive_system 3 1000
ATOM immune_system 3 950
ATOM skeletal_system 3 950
ATOM muscular_system 3 950
ATOM endocrine_system 3 900

IMP nervous_system organ_system FORMAL
IMP circulatory_system organ_system FORMAL
IMP respiratory_system organ_system FORMAL
IMP digestive_system organ_system FORMAL
IMP immune_system organ_system FORMAL
IMP skeletal_system organ_system FORMAL
IMP muscular_system organ_system FORMAL
IMP endocrine_system organ_system FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 9. Core biological processes
# ============================================================================

ATOM photosynthesis 3 1000
ATOM cellular_respiration 3 1000
ATOM mitosis 3 950
ATOM meiosis 3 950
ATOM protein_synthesis 3 950
ATOM evolution 3 1000
ATOM natural_selection 3 1000

IMP photosynthesis biological_process FORMAL
IMP cellular_respiration biological_process FORMAL
IMP mitosis biological_process FORMAL
IMP meiosis biological_process FORMAL
IMP protein_synthesis biological_process FORMAL
IMP evolution biological_process FORMAL
IMP natural_selection biological_process FORMAL

# Established mechanistic empirical claims
IMP photosynthesis chloroplast EMPIRICAL
IMP cellular_respiration mitochondria EMPIRICAL
IMP protein_synthesis ribosome EMPIRICAL
IMP natural_selection evolution EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 10. Foundational figures + historical milestones
# ============================================================================

ATOM darwin 1 950
ATOM mendel 1 950
ATOM watson 1 900
ATOM crick 1 900
ATOM franklin 1 900

IMP darwin person FORMAL
IMP mendel person FORMAL
IMP watson person FORMAL
IMP crick person FORMAL
IMP franklin person FORMAL

ATOM origin_of_species_1859 1 950
ATOM dna_structure_1953 1 950
ATOM mendel_pea_experiments 1 900

IMP origin_of_species_1859 historical_event FORMAL
IMP dna_structure_1953 historical_event FORMAL

IMP darwin origin_of_species_1859 EMPIRICAL
IMP watson dna_structure_1953 EMPIRICAL
IMP crick dna_structure_1953 EMPIRICAL
IMP franklin dna_structure_1953 EMPIRICAL
IMP mendel mendel_pea_experiments EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 11. Cross-source citations
# ============================================================================

CITE src:pack:biology:v1 src:paper:doi:campbell-biology-12e supports
CITE src:pack:biology:v1 src:paper:doi:alberts-molecular-biology-of-the-cell supports
CITE src:pack:biology:v1 src:paper:doi:ncbi-taxonomy-database supports
CITE src:pack:biology:v1 src:pack:physics:v1 extends
CITE src:pack:biology:v1 src:pack:world_history:v1 extends

# ============================================================================
# 12. Reinforcing observations for highest-confidence claims
# ============================================================================

OBS dna +1 1000
OBS evolution +1 1000
OBS photosynthesis +1 1000
OBS cellular_respiration +1 1000
